Follow the macOS system appearance for light/dark theming.

cosmic-term resolves its "System" app theme through libcosmic's
`theme::system_preference()`, which reads cosmic-config (`ThemeMode`). On macOS
that config does not exist, so it always falls back to dark and the terminal
ignores the real Aqua light/dark setting. libcosmic also only reacts to
cosmic-config theme-mode changes, so runtime appearance switches are missed too.

For the System variant, resolve the macOS appearance directly via
`defaults read -g AppleInterfaceStyle` (pinning `prefer_dark` so the cosmic-config
ThemeMode watcher does not force it back to dark), and add a subscription that
observes the `AppleInterfaceThemeChangedNotification` distributed notification —
registered on the main run loop via GCD — to re-apply the theme on every flip.

The macOS observer uses objc2 / objc2-foundation / block2 / dispatch2, which are
already in the dependency tree via winit on macOS, so the vendored crate set is
unchanged (only new dependency edges, resolved offline at build time). Everything
is `cfg(target_os = "macos")`-gated; no-op on Linux.

